SUMMARY:The Mummy (1932)
LOCATION:Kendall Square\, 355 Binney St\, Cambridge\, MA 02142
DESCRIPTION:Boris Karloff's legendary performance as The Mummy has become a
  landmark in the annals of screen history. When Egyptian mummy Im-Ho-Tep i
 s accidentally revived after 3\,700 years\, it is revealed in a flashback 
 that he was a high priest\, embalmed alive for trying to revive his true l
 ove after she had been sacrificed. Alive again\, he sets out on an obsessi
 ve - and deadly - quest to find his lost love. The Mummy remains a masterp
 iece not only of the genre\, but of all time.\nhttps://booking.landmarkthe
 atres.com/launch/ticketing/502dbb98-8e3f-5d6e-bc87-2262d6989fb8\nFrom Push
 pin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://booking.landmarktheatres.com/launch/ticketing/502dbb98-8e3f-5d6
 e-bc87-2262d6989fb8
END:VEVENT
